# SECRETS — this is the most important entry in this file.
#
# Verified: `next build` copies .env into .next/standalone/.env (709 bytes,
# containing SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY and SMTP_PASS). Without this exclusion,
# `COPY --from=builder /app/.next/standalone ./` bakes live credentials into an
# image layer — and layers stay extractable even if a later RUN deletes the file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build context size. Without these the daemon tars and streams ~2.1 GB on every
# build, and any change to either invalidates the `COPY . .` layer.
#   node_modules  822 MB  (the runner needs none of it: `output: "standalone"`
#                          traces the ~62 MB actually reachable at runtime)
#   .next         1.3 GB  (and the local copy was built on Windows with a D:\
#                          tracing root, so it is not even a Linux artifact)
node_modules
.next

# A stale tsbuildinfo makes `tsc --noEmit` silently SKIP files it believes are
# unchanged — a typecheck that checks nothing and exits 0.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Local queue state. Must never ship in an image, or a new replica could pick up
# and partially reprocess a stale queue. (Removed entirely in Stage 6.)
persistent_data
uploads

# Not needed at build or runtime
.git
.gitignore
.github
docs
deploy.sh
redeploy.sh
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.tar.gz
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
README.md
supabase_*.sql
